Job Description
The aim of the Monitoring and Evaluation (M&E) practice at DNA is to facilitate the systematic and independent measurement and assessment of project and programme design, implementation and performance. We conduct M&E with a strategic focus on enhancing performance, outcomes, and impact. We offer a diverse range of services that are customised to meet the specific needs of our clients. Our goal is to provide valuable insights and recommendations that contribute to improved performance, evidence-based decision-making, and enhanced learning within organisations.
DNA is looking for a senior monitoring and evaluation consultant to join our M&E practice. The Consultant will be responsible for undertaking M&E across a wide-range of sectors. Responsibilities will include:
Drafting evaluation proposals and designing M&E approaches and frameworks;
Leading and overseeing the implementation of multiple projects at any given time;
Developing data collection tools and fieldwork procedures;
Conducting quantitative and qualitative data analysis;
Compiling and writing evaluation reports;
Developing programme Theories of Change;
Presenting to and liaising with clients across a range of sectors;
Managing and mentoring junior evaluators;
Ensuring that projects are delivered in line with contract agreements and timelines;
Administrative responsibilities related to projects and company operations.
Requirements
