About the job:
The CSIR has a vacancy for a Telecommunications Engineer/Technologist: Artificial Intelligence (AI) in Heterogenous Wireless Technologies in the Spectrum Access and Management Innovation (SAMI) research within the Next Generation Enterprises and Institutions Cluster. The incumbent will be responsible to undertake research, design, develop, integrate, test, maintain and support a variety of technologies, applications, and systems relating to wireless communication and networks. This position is based in Pretoria.
Key responsibilities:
Conduct Research, Development and Innovation (RD&I) in heterogenous radio access network technologies ranging from terrestrial communication networks (e.g. next generation mobile networks, television white space networks, Wi-Fi) to airborne systems (e.g. using the Unmanned Arial Vehicles and satellite);
Contribute to the development and implementation bespoke operational programs as part of an overall system, for wireless communications networks and technologies;
Contribute to a team to develop, configure, test and validate code modules implementing system requirements to meet business needs;
Liaise with clients to understand and respond to their needs and requirements;
