Job Description:
Job Description
Truworths has an exciting opportunity for an Email Coder in our Marketing department. The Email Coder is responsible for coding, building/developing and testing email communications.
This role will be based at our Truworths Head Office in Cape Town.
Key Responsibilities
Utilize HTML and CSS to code marketing emails;
Set up and test complex email campaigns with dynamic content in the email software platform used by the business;
Apply the best practices in email development, email compliance regulations, and accessibility;
Perform QA on all coded emails;
Ensure identical rendering across browsers, ESPs, and devices;
Troubleshoot HTML, CSS, and other performance issues;
Proactively work with teammates to improve processes and work methods for greater efficiency;
Perform coding and database maintenance tasks as required.
Qualifications and Experience
Relevant tertiary qualification;
Relevant email development work experience, using html and css to code emails from scratch;
Experience working in one or more email tools to set up email templates;
Experience setting up dynamic content rules in email software.
Competencies
Advanced knowledge and understanding of HTML/CSS;
Proficient in responsive email design and front-end development;
Familiarity with email marketing and marketing automation technology;
A/B testing experience;
Knowledge of Google Analytics;
Experience with testing tools to ensure proper rendering across devices;
Works well under pressure;
Flexible;
Excellent attention to detail;
Good communication skills;
Team player.
go to method of application »

Purpose of the Job:
To regulate and supervise retirement funds and benefit administrators through monitoring compliance with the Pension Funds Act, Regulations, Board Notice 24 of 2002, Directives and FSCA’s policy to safeguard the interest of both the members of retirement funds and retirement fund benefit administrators. The person appointed to this position will report to the Manager.
Key Performance Areas:
Monitor compliance with legislation to ensure sound and efficient retirement funds and benefit administrators and to ensure the protection of consumers;
Analyse annual financial statements of retirement fund benefit administrators to ensure that proper reporting standards and procedures have been followed;
Analyse compliance reports and annual reports on retirement fund benefit administrators;
Liaise with retirement funds and benefit administrators on issues of non-compliance identified during desktop reviews, inspections and the analysis of compliance and annual reports;
Support team members with the analysis of regulatory returns;
Assist the Manager with projects and other ad hoc tasks;
Perform on-site inspections in terms of a risk-based supervision approach;
Produce on-site inspection reports on retirement funds and benefit administrators;
Assist the team with planning and on-site inspections;
Liaison with industry stakeholders; and
Perform administrative or other activities relating to the regulatory framework.
Requirements
A Bachelor of Commerce or Law degree with applicable working experience. Good knowledge and exposure to the Pension Funds Act and the industry will be an added advantage.
