RESPONSIBILITIES:
Approving, Controlling, monitoring, tracking of all non-routine and deferred maintenance activities (MEL, CDL etc.) to enable the aircraft to operate within the approved legal limits;
Update the Computer based Tracking Platform, Smart Sheet;
Support line personnel in trouble shooting for all maintenance defects/ MEL deferment;
Communication focal point between crew and engineers on all related defects, and also between aircraft and management for status reports required;
Track aircraft, follow up on daily status reports, and maintenance actions completed on the specific aircraft;
Coordinate the swapping of aircraft for technical reasons, and their towing to and from Hangers for maintenance;
Do the daily a/c scheduling first thing in the morning for the following day and pass on to Ops;
Coordinate requests from line, for requested parts with Logistics and engineering input in resolving any maintenance related issues;
Communicate to all outstations for feedback on any issues;
The Technical Line focal point for information on delays, cancellation of flights or maintenance related issues;
Follow up with Fault Analysis for trend monitoring and recurring defect rectification.
REQUIREMENTS:
Grade 12 Certificate or equivalent;
B737 experience;
Previous aviation experience in an operational area;
3-5 years’ experience on the line;
Previous experience with troubleshooting and fault finding;
Proficient in the use of Microsoft Office (Word, Excel and Outlook);
Willingness to work overtime when required.
PERSONAL ATTRIBUTES:
Detailed and able to work under pressure;
Able to follow instructions;
