Brief Description
The main purpose of this position is to provide specialist knowledge, skills and experience in the area of capital management and public disclosure as part of a team of specialists to ensure that the Prudential Authority (PA) fulfils its capital management responsibilities.
Detailed Description
The successful candidate will be responsible for the following key performance areas:
Review, analyse and evaluate banks’ internal capital-adequacy assessment process.
Review, analyse and evaluate insurers’ own risk and solvency assessment process.
Review and evaluate financial entities’ recovery plans.
Analyse and interpret risk-based regulatory returns for regulated entities.
Conduct research and provide input into the regulatory framework (e.g. the Banks Act 94 of 199 and Insurance Act 18 of 2017) in line with international best practice.
Interpret and develop amendments to the legislative framework based on international best practices.
Contribute towards international capital framework working committees.
Develop and implement the supervisory framework process in line with international best practice.
On-site reviews and assessments are conducted, which will require the candidate to travel.
Job Requirements
To be considered for this position, candidates must have:
a relevant degree (e.g. in banking, insurance, risk management, finance, accounting or auditing); and
more than five years’ applicable experience in the financial sector or in risk management.
The following would be an added advantage:
a postgraduate qualification in any of the aforementioned fields or certification as a Chartered Financial Analyst (CFA), Financial Risk Manager (FRM), Actuarial Society of South Africa (ASSA) associate (or an equivalent associate) or Chartered Accountant CA(SA); and practical experience in a financial and/or business environment.
Additional requirements include:
knowledge of, and experience in, financial, banking or insurance products, regulations, or risk models;
conversant in the second Pillar of the Basel III framework at both a theoretical and practical level and staying abreast of best practice in capital management;
an understanding of the Basel III framework regarding the definition of capital and leverage ratio;
conversant in the Insurance Act and its prudential standards and the information for supervisory purposes submitted by the insurance industry;
an understanding of the Insurance Core Principles, Guidance and Assessment Methodology;
a high level of knowledge, skills and experience in the relevant areas of specialisation;
able to work in a team;
being a self-starter;
effective time management;
proficiency in verbal communication;
competence in written communication; and
competence in Microsoft Office software packages.

