Purpose of the Job
To advise the Market Infrastructures and OTC Derivatives Providers internally on a wide range of practices, conduct and concerns affecting the industry and allied activities. The person appointed to this position will have a direct reporting line to the Senior Manager: OTC Market Supervision.
Requirements
A business, economics, accounting, mathematics degree or similar, with at least 5 years relevant experience, preferably in regulation, finance, risk management, audit or management consulting role within the South African Capital Markets Industry, finance or related commerce. Experience within a financial markets environment, investment banking, structured finance or similar will be a distinct advantage. An ability to understand complex financial instruments and processes including derivatives, bonds, equities and foreign exchange and the risks associated with these instruments would be desirable.
