To provide support to the Retirement Funds Supervision Division in their work by providing guidance on the manner in which to deal with specific cases; by providing input into the establishment, maintenance and monitoring of trustee training and qualifications and responsible for drafting and oversight of good governance principles and standards for funds. The person appointed to the position will report to the Manager.
Key Performance Areas:
Research local and international trends relating to good corporate governance;
Determine and evaluate funds’ compliance with the Treating Customers Fairly principles;
Responsible for coordinating and arranging workshops for retirement fund trustees;
Responsible for matters pertaining to the Trustee Training Toolkit
Research and evaluate issues relevant to fund governance and conduct of trustees of retirement funds;
Provide general legal support to the departments within the Retirement Funds Supervision Division;
Draft responses to Default Regulation Exemptions and Extensions
Propose and draft Guidance Notices and Conduct Standards in terms of the FSRA;
Provide input into the establishment, maintenance and monitoring of trustee training and qualifications (where applicable);
Assist the Retirement Funds Supervision Division with the implementation of appropriate enforcement actions provided for in Chapter 10 of the FSRA.
Closing Date: 15 August 2023

